# PG-EOS — never commit secrets, keys, dumps or backups (CLAUDE.md · GIT).
# BOOTSTRAP-v4 §9 names the first seven entries; the rest are build output.

# ── secrets and credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_*
!id_*.ts
!id_*.tsx

# ── data, dumps, backups ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/
*.dump
*.tgz
*.sql.gz
*.bak

# ── dependencies and build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.turbo/
coverage/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── test and tool artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
playwright-report/
test-results/
reports/mutation/
.stryker-tmp/

# ── editor and OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── NOT ignored, deliberately ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# .golden-slice-accepted  — the GM's acceptance record for WBS 2.9. It IS COMMITTED:
#   scripts/new-slice.sh stays a no-op until this file exists in the repository, so a
#   local-only copy would let one machine replicate while the others could not.
#   Never add it here (BOOTSTRAP-v5 §9 · EXECUTION-MASTER-v4 §3.5).
# .claude/                — agents, commands, briefs, hooks and settings are the kit and are
#   versioned with the code. Only .claude/settings.local.json is personal:
.claude/settings.local.json
